problems.q:
Inputs a, b, c; g1 = AND(a, c); g2 = NOR(b, g1); g3 = NAND(a, g2); g4 = AND(b, g3); g5 = NAND(g1, g4); primary output g5. Targeting b stuck-at-1, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = X, b = 0, c = 0 and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g2}

B) {g4}

C) {g3, g4}

D) {g2, g3, g4}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = NAND(b, c); g2 = NOR(a, g1); g3 = AND(c, g2); g4 = OR(a, g3); g5 = NAND(g2, g4); primary output g5. Targeting a stuck-at-1, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = 0, b = X, c = X and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g2, g3, g4}

B) {g1, g2, g4}

C) {g2, g4}

D) {g1}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = OR(a, b); g2 = AND(b, g1); g3 = NOR(b, g2); g4 = OR(c, g3); g5 = OR(a, g4); primary output g5. Targeting g3 stuck-at-0, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = X, b = 0, c = X and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g4, g5}

B) {g4}

C) {g1, g4}

D) {g1}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = NAND(b, c); g2 = OR(c, g1); g3 = NOR(g1, g2); g4 = AND(a, b); g5 = AND(b, g4); primary outputs g3 and g5. The D-algorithm has assigned a = 1, c = 1, g3 = 0, g5 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g1}

B) {g1, g5}

C) {g3, g5}

D) {g5}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = NAND(a, c); g2 = AND(b, g1); g3 = NAND(c, g2); g4 = NOR(c, g3); g5 = NOR(g2, g4); primary output g5. The D-algorithm has assigned a = 1, b = 1, g1 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g3}

B) {g1}

C) {g1, g4}

D) {g1, g3}

Inputs a, b, c, d; g1 = NAND(c, d); g2 = AND(b, g1); g3 = NOR(c, g2); g4 = OR(a, b); g5 = NOR(d, g4); g6 = AND(g3, g5); primary output g6. The D-algorithm has assigned a = 0, c = 1, g3 = 0, g4 = 0, g5 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g1, g4, g5}

B) {g2, g4, g5}

C) {g4, g5}

D) {g1}
